## 🔥 Choose ONE High-Impact Skill You Can Learn *Today* in CS

### ✅ My pick: **Build a REST API in Node.js (with MongoDB)**

**Why?**
- You'll learn backend logic, routes, databases, JSON — **real-world dev stuff**
- It’s used in internships, full-stack apps, and interviews
- You’ll *build something tangible* in a few hours

---

## 🛠️ What You’ll Build Today:
> A simple **"Note-Taking API"** — you can Create, Read, Update, and Delete notes (CRUD)

---

## 🧠 What You’ll Learn in 1 Day:
| Skill Area         | What You’ll Learn                        |
|--------------------|------------------------------------------|
| Backend (Node.js)  | Express.js basics, middleware            |
| API design         | RESTful endpoints                        |
| MongoDB            | Mongoose models and queries              |
| JSON & HTTP        | Request/Response cycle                   |
| Postman/ThunderClient | API testing (real-time feedback)       |

---

## ⚙️ Tools You Need:
- Node.js & npm
- MongoDB Atlas (free cloud DB)
- VS Code
- Postman (or ThunderClient extension)

---

## 🚀 Step-by-Step Plan for Today:

### **Hour 1: Setup**
- Install Node.js + MongoDB
- Init project:
  ```bash
  mkdir notes-api && cd notes-api
  npm init -y
  npm install express mongoose dotenv
  ```

### **Hour 2: Create Server + Connect DB**
```js
// server.js
const express = require('express');
const mongoose = require('mongoose');
const dotenv = require('dotenv');
dotenv.config();

const app = express();
app.use(express.json());

mongoose.connect(process.env.MONGO_URI, { useNewUrlParser: true })
  .then(() => console.log('MongoDB connected'));

app.get('/', (req, res) => res.send('API is working'));

app.listen(5000, () => console.log('Server running on 5000'));
```

### **Hour 3: Make a Note Model**
```js
// models/Note.js
const mongoose = require('mongoose');

const noteSchema = new mongoose.Schema({
  title: String,
  content: String,
});

module.exports = mongoose.model('Note', noteSchema);
```

### **Hour 4–5: Create Routes (CRUD)**
```js
// routes/noteRoutes.js
const express = require('express');
const router = express.Router();
const Note = require('../models/Note');

// Create Note
router.post('/', async (req, res) => {
  const note = new Note(req.body);
  const saved = await note.save();
  res.json(saved);
});

// Get All Notes
router.get('/', async (req, res) => {
  const notes = await Note.find();
  res.json(notes);
});

// Update Note
router.put('/:id', async (req, res) => {
  const updated = await Note.findByIdAndUpdate(req.params.id, req.body, { new: true });
  res.json(updated);
});

// Delete Note
router.delete('/:id', async (req, res) => {
  await Note.findByIdAndDelete(req.params.id);
  res.json({ message: 'Deleted' });
});

module.exports = router;
```

Hook the router in `server.js`:
```js
const noteRoutes = require('./routes/noteRoutes');
app.use('/api/notes', noteRoutes);
```

### **Hour 6: Test it in Postman**
- POST `/api/notes` → Add new note
- GET `/api/notes` → View notes
- PUT `/api/notes/:id` → Update
- DELETE `/api/notes/:id` → Delete

